+# UMS explosive-material allegation: vehicle sampling, two controls and missing final chemistry
+
+**This source test identifies a vehicle-related sampling trail, not a confirmed explosive substance on any individual.** It preserves an object-description mismatch, separates chemical testing from unrelated positive/negative/pending wording, and acquires official FBI request-log records that offer additional retrieval routes. No original canine-handler report, laboratory submission/accession, analytical data or final chemical disposition was obtained. The test of confirmed explosive material remains **open**.
+
+Existing research keys: **UMC09 / M113**, with **UMC07** for item/person attribution. Company control, government employment, intelligence affiliation, tasking and attack participation remain separate **UMC10** questions. The earlier [six-question/eleven-chain review](../record-chains-2026-10-26/README.md) and original source bytes remain unchanged. This note reports a selected source comparison and new administrative records, not experimental replication or completion of an attack hypothesis.
+
+## What the original pages actually say
+
+| Source and exact locator | Observation retained | Evidentiary limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| [Part5, physical43](https://archive.org/download/fbinewarkdivisionfullfieldinvestigation/FBI%20Newark%20Division%20Full-Field%20Investigation%20Part%205.pdf#page=43), opening header; **physical44/printed2**, penultimate substantive paragraph | The account is dated **September23,2001**. It reports a trained bomb-sniffing dog's positive result concerning the **vehicle**, swabs of its **interior**, transmission to the FBI laboratory and final results still pending. | An investigator's summary of a canine indication and submission is not the handler's original deployment record or chemical identification. The sentence does not report a substance, concentration, analytical method or person-positive test. Pending refers to this dated account, not a verified current status. |
+| [Serial325 p2](https://www.israellobby.org/UrbanMoving/1169683-001%20---%20303A-NY-C237934-Serial%20325%20---%20Section%201%20%281037758%29.pdf#page=2), first Details paragraph | The October17 account instead describes a **possible hit** received by a law-enforcement bomb-squad canine. | Preserve the stronger positive-result wording beside possible-hit wording. They may describe the same event and are not two independently documented alerts. No cause for the wording difference is selected. |
+| [Part1 physical7](https://archive.org/download/fbinewarkdivisionfullfieldinvestigation/FBI%20Newark%20Division%20Full-Field%20Investigation%20Part%201.pdf#page=7), FD-192 source/acquisition fields and bottom three barcode groups | Source field identifies **NJ LICENSE JRJ13Y**; Date Property Acquired is **09/12/2001**. The form's separate header prints **07/29/03 09:58:33**. Item15 is a fabric sample labelled explosive residue;16 and17 are explicitly control swabs;34 is blanket samples for explosive residue. | Acquisition date, form-generation label and actual sampling time are different fields. A vehicle-source inventory field is a useful join, not a complete item-by-item collection/custody record or a person-specific chemical finding. |
+| [Part6 physical42–43/printed5–6](https://archive.org/download/fbinewarkdivisionfullfieldinvestigation/FBI%20Newark%20Division%20Full-Field%20Investigation%20Part%206.pdf#page=42), paragraph spanning the page break | The counterpart repeats the vehicle/dog/swab account and says samples were sent to the **crime laboratory**. The corresponding paragraph does not contain Part5's final-results-still-pending sentence. | Preserve the differing wording. This is neither a final result nor proof testing finished, failed, was cancelled or concealed. It does not identify an accession or explain the change from FBI laboratory to crime laboratory. Other parts of the case were not exhaustively reviewed. |
+
+The apparent FBI release PDFs are public-mirror scans. Their held bytes match the earlier manifests, but a complete authenticated chain from the FBI release to these mirrors is not established. The official FBI logs below have agency-hosted provenance, but they do not authenticate the substantive mirrored case files.
+
+## Four item descriptions do not equal four positive chemical findings
+
+The actual Part1 p7 inventory supplies **four numbered descriptions under three barcode groups**:
+
+| Item | Literal description, with redacted identity omitted | Barcode | What remains needed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+|15|FABRIC SAMPLE (EXPLOSIVE RESIDUE)|E01889035|Exact fabric/location/source, collection worksheet, submission and final result.|
+|16|CONTROL SWABS - SA [redacted] GLOVES|E01889036|Collection/handling relationship, control result and comparison to questioned samples.|
+|17|CONTROL SWABS - (BOMB SUITS)|E01889036|Same; do not assign an undisclosed wearer or positive result.|
+|34|BLANKET SAMPLES FOR EXPLOSIVE RESIDUE|E01889037|Exact blanket/source/location, sampling worksheet, submission and final result.|
+
+Two descriptions are **controls**, including gloves attributed to an SA, rather than four established suspect-positive specimens. None of these inventory labels is an acquired analytical report. Whether the fabric label reflects a suspected trace, preliminary assessment or established identification cannot be determined from the inventory alone. Likewise, controls do not prove contamination occurred or that all samples were clean. Their results are missing.
+
+The summary's search of the van and occupants must not be expanded into a finding that explosives were chemically detected **on the five men**. The chemical-related paragraph specifically describes the vehicle and interior swabs. An item/person or material/operation attribution requires additional evidence.
+
+## New object-description mismatch: blankets absent versus blanket samples inventoried
+
+The next page of the same September23 summary, [Part5 physical45/printed3](https://archive.org/download/fbinewarkdivisionfullfieldinvestigation/FBI%20Newark%20Division%20Full-Field%20Investigation%20Part%205.pdf#page=45), first paragraph, says equipment typically used in a moving company's daily duties was not found, expressly including **work gloves, blankets, straps, ropes, boxes, dollies and rollers**. The Part1 inventory nevertheless lists **blanket samples**.
+
+Keep both statements. They create an unresolved **object/scope/source correspondence question**: what material was sampled, where and when was it obtained, and what objects did the summary's not-found account cover? A retained fragment or sample versus usable equipment, a different collection context/date, or an inaccurate description are possible tests, not resolved explanations. Neither source alone establishes planted material, a false laboratory result, a substituted vehicle or deliberate misstatement. The original search inventory/photos, sampling worksheet, sample envelopes and submission manifest would discriminate. The SA-glove controls are not automatically the work gloves described as missing.
+
+## Negative and pending passages concern different examinations
+
+- [Part5 physical47/printed5](https://archive.org/download/fbinewarkdivisionfullfieldinvestigation/FBI%20Newark%20Division%20Full-Field%20Investigation%20Part%205.pdf#page=47), paragraph beginning Based upon the aforementioned facts: the **September13 office search** met with **negative results concerning a video camera**. This is not a negative chemical finding.
+- [Serial326 physical2](https://www.israellobby.org/UrbanMoving/1169683-001%20---%20303A-NY-C237934-Serial%20326%20---%20Section%201%20%281037759%29.pdf#page=2), first long paragraph after the continuation: the **October19,2001** memo describes preliminary Quantico computer-hard-drive analysis around October10, a later removable-media search and **analysis of obtained flash medium pending**. It is not the explosive-swab result.
+- The **chemical pending** statement is the separate Part5 physical44 paragraph dated through its September23 header. Neither pending passage establishes today's disposition. A later administrative instruction to discontinue laboratory leads, described in the earlier review, also cannot substitute for a specimen-specific result.
+
+These are controls against keyword conflation. The selected-source test excludes two tempting but inapplicable passages; it does not settle the missing chemical question.
+
+## Newly acquired official FBI logs identify three different request routes
+
+The actual agency-hosted PDFs, not just search snippets, were downloaded and hashed. Extraction screened only for Urban Moving to locate candidate pages; the **three resulting full page images** were then read, with only the relevant rows transcribed here.
+
+| Official source and physical page | FOIA number / revision | Date Opened | Subject exactly as displayed |
+|---|---|---|---|
+|[2018 log p23](https://vault.fbi.gov/foia-log-2018-part-01/FOIA%20Log%202018%20Part%2001%20%28Final%29/#page=23)|1423771 /000|10-Dec-2018|Urban Moving Systems|
+|[2018 log p257](https://vault.fbi.gov/foia-log-2018-part-01/FOIA%20Log%202018%20Part%2001%20%28Final%29/#page=257)|1408889 /000|20-Jun-2018|Photos taken by employees of Urban Moving Systems|
+|[2022 log p127](https://vault.fbi.gov/foia-log-2022-part-01/FOIA%20Log%202022%20Part%2001%20%28Final%29/#page=127)|1568844 /000|19-Oct-2022|Urban Moving Systems|
+
+These are **request-log entries**, not proof of a completed release, a still-open request, its full scope, surviving responsive records or laboratory results. The photo request is a separate possible route to surviving visual evidence; it is not a chemical-result request merely because it concerns the same company. Request numbers repeated in later annual logs must not be counted as independent case evidence or additional requests. No requester identity is inferred or needed here.
+
+Exact-number public searches did not acquire a linked determination/production containing a final chemical result. Those searches are bounded and are not an exhaustive search of all FBI or local police holdings. The logs give concrete reference identifiers for finding already public responses or later retrieval; no new request or contact was made.
+
+## Actual scope and open tests
+
+**Read now:** Part5 physical43–47, Part6 physical42–43 and the three official-log pages: **ten page images**. **Reinspected counterparts:** Part1p7, Serial325p2, Serial326p2 and Part6p40: **four previously rendered pages**. Part6p40 was inspected as adjacent closing-account context, not relied on as chemical findings. Other substantive case pages were not newly read in full.
+
+Held archive OCR/XML for Parts1/3/5 and search-only text for Parts2/4/6 were used only to locate terms. Part6's XML was newly downloaded to locate42–43. OCR incompleteness/redaction prevents a corpus-wide negative-result claim. The two full official logs were screened by text extraction for the target subject, not read in full. No raw specimens, native instrument files, handler records or laboratory accession were acquired, and no chemical experiment, signature authentication or redaction reconstruction was performed.
+
+The strongest adverse interpretation would require an authenticated substance-specific result, controls and custody tied to an identified person/vehicle and relevant operational activity. Strong contrary evidence could be a matched negative/inconclusive finding, reliable non-explosive explanation of the alert or a different documented specimen origin. None is adopted without the corresponding records. Even confirmed material and intelligence control would require separate timing, possession, use and attack-connection tests; these records establish neither premise together nor manipulation of al-Qaeda.
+
+[Source pins](SOURCES.json), [specimen/result crosswalk](SPECIMEN-RESULT-CROSSWALK.json), [bounded search log](SEARCH-LOG.json), [open tests](OPEN-TODOS.json), [review checklist](REVIEW-AND-CHECKS.json) and [exact additive text diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) accompany this note. Earlier records remain unchanged. The original five-track investigation and its missing inputs remain open; this UMS unit does not complete FAA correction/disposition, telephone, recorder, materials or steel tests.
